Pipeline owns a Process and its requested output file path.
initialize creates the Process and empty output path.
process returns the underlying Process. environment: and input: configure environment overrides and first-stage input before launch.
start:cwd:outputFile: accepts an Array of nonempty argument Arrays, a working directory and optional final output file path.
    Each stage uses literal executable and string arguments, connected by operating-system pipes.
    An empty output path captures final standard output; a nonempty path streams final bytes into a created or truncated file.
outputFile returns the configured destination. stdout, stderr, output and outputLines expose bounded captured text.
status, error and command describe the aggregate job. exitCode is the rightmost nonzero stage exit, or zero if all succeed; exitCodes returns each stage's exit code in order.
wait returns the aggregate exit code. signal: addresses all stage process groups; stop requests termination.
inspectorMetadata supplies status, exit and destination properties. inspectorViews supplies commands, output streams, errors and actions for stage exits and stop.
